	1.	Identify the problem – Clearly understand what needs to be solved.
	2.	Research the problem – Collect information about users, existing solutions, and requirements.
	3.	Generate ideas – Think of as many possible solutions as possible without judging them initially.
	4.	Discuss and improve ideas – Compare ideas and combine useful features.
	5.	Evaluate ideas – Check each idea based on feasibility, cost, usefulness, time, and technology.
	6.	Select the best idea – Choose the solution that is most practical and valuable.
	7.	Define the concept – Clearly describe the selected idea and its main features.
